---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Downloads — Tempo"
  description="Everything you can download for Tempo — the app itself, scores, and utilities."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1>Downloads</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Tempo is the app, but it's not the whole story. Scores teach Tempo about
      your sources; utilities fit alongside Tempo to fill workflow gaps. Pick
      what you need.
    </p>
  </header>

  <main class="cards">

    <article class="card">
      <h2>Tempo</h2>
      <p class="card-desc">
        A Mac-native event hub. One Mac-native timeline for everything your
        stack does — from rack-side monitoring to Mac-side automations, from
        third-party services to your own scripts. If it can POST, Tempo can
        hear it. Every event arrives in context, with the next move one
        click away. You stay the conductor; Tempo holds the score — and
        never acts on its own.
      </p>
      <p class="card-meta">
        macOS 15+ · Signed + notarized DMG · No App Store · Auto-updates via Sparkle
      </p>
      <p class="card-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://downloads.tempoapp.app/Tempo-latest.dmg">Download DMG</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/blog/">Read the blog</a>
      </p>

      <details class="install-alt">
        <summary>Or install via Homebrew</summary>
        <pre><code>brew tap caereforge/tap
brew install --cask tempo</code></pre>
        <p class="install-alt-note">
          Same signed + notarized DMG, distributed through a public Homebrew
          tap. Updates flow through Sparkle as usual; <code>brew upgrade --cask tempo</code>
          works too if you prefer the Homebrew flow. Tap source:
          <a href="https://github.com/caereforge/homebrew-tap">github.com/caereforge/homebrew-tap</a>.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="install-alt">
        <summary>Verify your download</summary>
        <p class="install-alt-note">
          The DMG is signed and notarized with Caereforge's Developer ID, so macOS
          Gatekeeper verifies authenticity automatically on first launch. For an
          additional integrity check from a terminal:
        </p>
        <pre><code>shasum -a 256 Tempo-latest.dmg</code></pre>
        <p class="install-alt-note">Expected SHA-256 for the current release:</p>
        <pre><code>cf4ba0fd858f912ffb2f339ef52c1002e42c8dc6a21defee2e63f96d1fa3fe40</code></pre>
      </details>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h2>Scores</h2>
      <p class="card-desc">
        Small declarative JSON files that teach Tempo about a source — the
        color, the severity rules, and the one-click actions to attach. Drop
        one in, the source is wired up.
      </p>
      <p class="card-meta">
        Tempo ships with a core set bundled in. The catalog below adds
        downloadable extras for tools the bundle doesn't cover.
      </p>
      <p class="card-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/scores/">Browse the catalog</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="https://github.com/caereforge/tempo-scores">Source on GitHub</a>
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h2>Utilities</h2>
      <p class="card-desc">
        Shortcuts, scripts, and small helper tools that complement Tempo. They
        don't define a Tempo source — they fit alongside, filling the workflow
        gaps that the app itself doesn't try to solve.
      </p>
      <p class="card-meta">
        First entry: a macOS Shortcut to copy <code>message://</code> deep
        links from Apple Mail. More land as the catalog grows.
      </p>
      <p class="card-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/caereforge/tempo-utilities">Browse on GitHub</a>
      </p>
    </article>

  </main>

  <footer class="page-footer">
    <p>
      Looking for documentation? See the <a href="/blog/">blog</a> for design
      notes, dev logs, and walkthroughs.
    </p>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.25rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .page-nav {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .page-nav a { color: var(--text2); }
  .page-nav a:hover { color: var(--text); }

  .page-header h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .lede {
    color: var(--text2);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .cards {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem 4rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .card {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--bg-elev, transparent);
  }

  .card h2 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
  }

  .card-desc {
    color: var(--text2);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .card-meta {
    color: var(--text3);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .card-meta code {
    background: var(--bg-elev, rgba(0,0,0,0.05));
    padding: 0.1rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }

  .card-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .install-alt {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  .install-alt summary {
    color: var(--text2);
    cursor: pointer;
    user-select: none;
    padding: 0.25rem 0;
  }
  .install-alt summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .install-alt[open] summary {
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .install-alt pre {
    background: var(--bg-elev, rgba(0,0,0,0.04));
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .install-alt pre code {
    background: transparent;
    padding: 0;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  }
  .install-alt-note {
    color: var(--text3);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
  .install-alt-note code {
    background: var(--bg-elev, rgba(0,0,0,0.05));
    padding: 0.1rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    font-size: 0.95em;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  }
  .install-alt-note a { color: var(--blue); }

  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.9rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: background 0.15s, color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background: var(--blue);
    color: var(--bg);
  }
  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: var(--blue-hover, var(--blue));
    filter: brightness(1.05);
  }

  .btn-secondary {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text2);
    background: transparent;
  }
  .btn-secondary:hover {
    color: var(--text);
    border-color: var(--text2);
  }

  .page-footer {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.25rem 4rem;
    color: var(--text3);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .page-footer a { color: var(--blue); }
</style>
